WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.747
Metacognition makes learning more active.

00:00:01.747 --> 00:00:05.369
Instead of passively consuming content, the learner plans practice, monitors progress,

00:00:05.369 --> 00:00:08.333
uses retrieval, spaces review, seeks feedback, and adjusts methods.

00:00:08.333 --> 00:00:12.284
The learner asks what capability is being built and what evidence would

00:00:12.284 --> 00:00:14.260
show that the capability is real.

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:17.224
This keeps learning connected to performance instead of completion.

00:00:17.224 --> 00:00:20.517
Planning practice means choosing the skill and the exercise deliberately.

00:00:20.517 --> 00:00:22.493
If the goal is better troubleshooting,

00:00:22.493 --> 00:00:25.457
practice may focus on hypothesis formation or evidence collection.

00:00:25.457 --> 00:00:30.067
If the goal is better writing, practice may focus on outlining or revising claims.

00:00:30.067 --> 00:00:32.043
If the goal is better communication,

00:00:32.043 --> 00:00:35.336
practice may focus on summarizing uncertainty or asking clearer questions.

00:00:35.336 --> 00:00:38.629
Monitoring progress means noticing whether the current method is working.

00:00:38.629 --> 00:00:39.617
Are errors repeating?

00:00:39.617 --> 00:00:42.252
Is the learner retrieving the idea without looking?

00:00:42.252 --> 00:00:45.545
Is the task too easy, too hard, or productively challenging?

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:47.191
Has feedback identified a bottleneck?

00:00:47.191 --> 00:00:51.143
A metacognitive learner adjusts difficulty and strategy instead of assuming that more

00:00:51.143 --> 00:00:54.436
time with the same method will automatically solve the problem.

00:00:54.436 --> 00:00:57.729
This also helps learners know when to ask for help.

00:00:57.729 --> 00:01:02.010
Asking for help is more effective when the learner can name the target,

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:04.316
the attempt, the gap, and the uncertainty.

00:01:04.316 --> 00:01:08.267
Instead of saying, I do not get it, the learner can say,

00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:09.914
I can follow the example,

00:01:09.914 --> 00:01:13.207
but I cannot choose the method on a new problem.

00:01:13.207 --> 00:01:16.500
That is a much better starting point for useful feedback.
